{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795248200,"nonce":"wW6w88+H0rKs56pgXinfY8pZBF8=","title":"Inset box shadows never paint in the windowed renderer","message":"GitHub #86. `box-shadow: 0 0 20px #b8bcb5 inset` on a div has no visible effect in a windowed app, in 0.6.0 and on main.\n\nThe value parses and reaches `RenderNode::props.inner_shadow`, but only the simple paint walk (`paint/basic.rs`) calls `draw_inner_shadow`. The paths the window and the headless harness use (`paint/motion.rs`, `paint/layered.rs`, `paint/layout_renderer.rs`) draw the outer stack only. e15ee566 added inset painting to `basic.rs` alone; its test draws on a canvas directly, so it never went through the element paint walk.\n\nReproducer: a headless render of the issue's snippet shows the border and no inset; a solid red inset, a background, or no border change nothing.\n\nSecond defect in the same snippet: a rule whose `box-shadow` has no inset layer (the issue's `:hover`) leaves an inset from an earlier rule in place. `stylesheet/apply.rs` writes `inner_shadow` only when the list is non-empty, so the hover state cannot clear it; in CSS the declaration replaces both.","files":null}]}